{"id":"G2074","lemma":"Ἐσρώμ","transliteration":"esrōm","sayIt":"ESRŌM","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"","gloss":"Hezron","meaning":"Ἑσρώμ\n(Ἑσρών, Lk, l.with; Rec. Ἑσρ-), ὁ (Heb. חֶצְרוֹן, Gen.46:12, Num.26:21, 1Ch.25:1-31, al.), [in LXX both forms, ut supr. (cf. ICC, on Mt, l.with; WH, § 408) ;]\nEsrom (AV), Hezron (RV), an ancestor of Jesus: Mat.13:1-58, Luk.3:35.†\n(AS)","glosses":["hezron"],"count":2,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-1","v":3,"renderings":{"bsb":"Hezron","kjv":"Esrom"}},{"chapterId":"luk-3","v":33,"renderings":{"bsb":"of Hezron","kjv":"which was the son of Esrom"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Matthew 1:3","note":"Judah became the father of Perez and Zerah by Tamar. Perez became the father of Hezron. Hezron became the father of Ram.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Luke 3:33","note":"the son of Amminadab, the son of Aram, the son of Hezron, the son of Perez, the son of Judah,","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"H2696","lemma":"חֶצְרוֹן","transliteration":"chetsron","gloss":"Hezron"},{"id":"G20740","lemma":"μισθαρχίδης","transliteration":"mistharchidēs","gloss":"mercenary"},{"id":"G20741","lemma":"μισοξενία","transliteration":"misoxenia","gloss":"guests"},{"id":"G20742","lemma":"μισοπονηρέω","transliteration":"misoponēreō","gloss":"to hate wickedness"},{"id":"G20743","lemma":"μισοπονηρία","transliteration":"misoponēria","gloss":"hatred because of wickedness"},{"id":"G20744","lemma":"μισοπόνηρος","transliteration":"misoponēros","gloss":"with hostile sentiments"},{"id":"G20745","lemma":"μίσυβρις","transliteration":"misubris","gloss":"hating insolence"},{"id":"G20746","lemma":"Μίτρα","transliteration":"mitra","gloss":"Mitra"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}